  "title": "Compound individuals and aggregational societies",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "71160dfb-d1d8-4618-beae-fad2ca7120b7",
      "text": "A compound individual, such as an animal, is a society of occasions in which a higher-level actuality has emerged, giving the whole a unity of experience and activity. An aggregational society, such as a rock, has no such dominant occasion.",
